<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1441" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδο-λέσχης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prater, idle talker</i>, esp. of reputed sophists: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σωκράτην, τὸν πτωχὸν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					352
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1485
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ Πρόδικος ἢ τῶν ἀ. εἷς γέ τις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					490
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τις σοφιστής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					299b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tht.</u>
				195b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				488e
			</span></i>: generally, <i>talker, babbler</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				3.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1117b35
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in good
			sense, <i>subtle reasoner</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				401b
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ-</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> ll. c.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁδέω,
		λέσχη.</span>]</div>
